refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public Io\Poll\Context::__construct Io\Poll\BackendbackendIo\Poll\Backend::Auto
Creates a polling context that uses the given backend.

&reftitle.parameters;
backend
The polling mechanism to use. With Io\Poll\Backend::Auto, the most suitable backend available on the platform is selected; Io\Poll\Context::getBackend tells which one it is.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws an Io\Poll\BackendUnavailableException if backend is not available on the platform.
Throws an Io\Poll\FailedContextInitializationException if the backend cannot be initialized.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Io\Poll\Context::__construct example


<?php
use Io\Poll\Backend;
use Io\Poll\BackendUnavailableException;
use Io\Poll\Context;

$context = new Context();
var_dump($context->getBackend());

try {
    $context = new Context(Backend::WSAPoll);
} catch (BackendUnavailableException $exception) {
    echo $exception->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


   &example.outputs.similar;


enum(Io\Poll\Backend::Epoll)
Backend WSAPoll not available
